menu "RBgrid"

config RBGRID_DEBUG_BRIDGE
    bool "Enable rbbench debug bridge console (HW test/debug)"
    default n
    help
        Compile the rbbench debug-bridge console into RBgrid (the test-rig
        harness). Exposes a UART0 BRIDGE_SHELL line protocol with i2c/load/meter
        verbs plus RBgrid introspection verbs, for hardware-in-the-loop testing
        (load sweeps, reference meter, flash diagnostics). Off in production.
        When enabled, RBgrid also starts the rbAmp bridge (to provide the shared
        sensor I2C bus handle) and lowers the log level so the console stays clean.

config RBGRID_BENCH_FULL
    bool "Unified bench build (rbbench console + wifi/telemetry together)"
    default n
    help
        Compile the rbbench debug-bridge console (load/meter/i2cscan
        verbs) ALONGSIDE the full wifi/telemetry/MQTT stack in one image. PSRAM
        removed the RAM/console split that used to force them apart, so the stand
        can drive controlled loads AND validate the live telemetry pipeline from a
        single build. Unlike RBGRID_DEBUG_BRIDGE this keeps wifi ON. Off in
        production. Set ESP_CONSOLE_NONE so rbbench owns the UART0 driver (app logs
        still emit via the ROM printf path).

endmenu
